\import{ftip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\taxon{Example}
\title{A retained build-repair trace}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{evaluation}

\p{The horizon and selective-refinement observations in
\citet{Sections 3-7}{dang2026selecting} motivate the following finite
classification. Consider a run whose task is to repair a failing build. The retained record
contains the failing observation, the source edit, a test execution, and a
final verifier pass. With the event interface of \ref{ftip-00P6}, the test and
verification steps contribute to #{e_{\rm ev}}, #{e_{\rm pass}}, and
#{n_{\rm prod}}, so the record can satisfy #{\operatorname{Prod}(T)}.}

\p{If the test event is removed from the retained record, the same token budget
can fail the productive predicate because the evidence chain is incomplete.
If identical shell retries continue after #{\tau_{\rm sat}} with no new
productive event, #{\operatorname{Over}(T)} can hold. This is a finite
classification example; it does not claim that every short trace is better or
that a model has an inner persistence objective.}
